  "body": "## Wallpaper Reactor 0.30.0\n\n_Changes since 0.29.0_\n\n## Highlights\n\n### All platforms\n\n- Performance modes are now free for everyone\n- You can upload scenes, interactive 3D (Godot) and website wallpapers\n\n### Linux\n\n- Wallpaper Reactor now sets wallpapers on KDE Plasma 5, GNOME 46+ on Wayland, Sway and Hyprland, as well as KDE Plasma 6, with the .deb and the Flatpak\n\n### Windows\n\n- Wallpaper Reactor now has its own title bar on Windows, with Snap Layouts on the maximize button\n\n### macOS\n\n- You can now buy Pro in the Mac App Store version\n\n## Features\n\n### All platforms\n\n- A new log screen with a level filter, search, follow, copy and refresh, and export to a file named with the date and version\n- Keyboard shortcuts for the whole app, with a ? sheet that lists them\n- Icon-only controls show a tooltip\n- The Create screen uses two columns when the window is wide\n- Menus open with the same motion everywhere\n- The details screen no longer shows the account button\n\n### Android\n\n- Wallpaper Reactor works on Android devices that use 16 KB memory pages\n- Files you open with or share to Wallpaper Reactor are picked up directly, and you can drop a file on the window in desktop mode\n- Fullscreen mode on Android 15 and later, with F11 on a keyboard\n- After a crash, the app offers to send a crash report, and sending is optional\n- Returning from the background keeps the last frame on screen until the app has drawn again\n- A fresh install reaches onboarding without waiting on the splash screen\n\n### Windows\n\n- The wallpaper helper has a notification-area icon with Open, Reload and Close\n- A new setting makes the Windows accent color follow your wallpaper, off by default\n- Taskbar icons now have versions made for the light theme\n- In the Microsoft Store version, choosing Close from the notification-area icon also stops Wallpaper Reactor from starting at sign-in until you start it again\n\n### Linux\n\n- Wallpaper Reactor now has its own title bar on Linux, with drag, resize and double-click to maximize on KDE Plasma\n\n## Removed\n\n- Create → Picture, the old picture editor\n\n## Fixes\n\n### All platforms\n\n- Fixed the Browse shelves and results not filling the screen after the window was resized\n\n### Android\n\n- Fixed the app never finishing loading on some devices with an older Android 12 WebView\n\n### Windows\n\n- Fixed Expand mode pausing the wallpaper before every display it spans was covered\n\n## Downloads\n\n| Platform | Get it |\n| --- | --- |\n| Android | [Google Play](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=app.wallpaperreactor) · [APK](https://github.com/wallpaper-reactor/wallpaper-reactor-website/releases/download/v0.30.0/wallpaper-reactor-v0.30.0-android.apk) |\n| Windows | [Microsoft Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9N4302CRDQRL) · [Installer (.exe)](https://github.com/wallpaper-reactor/wallpaper-reactor-website/releases/download/v0.30.0/wallpaper-reactor-v0.30.0-windows-x64-setup.exe) · [.msi](https://github.com/wallpaper-reactor/wallpaper-reactor-website/releases/download/v0.30.0/wallpaper-reactor-v0.30.0-windows-x64.msi) |\n| macOS | [Mac App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/wallpaper-reactor-lite/id6751447022) · [.dmg](https://github.com/wallpaper-reactor/wallpaper-reactor-website/releases/download/v0.30.0/wallpaper-reactor-v0.30.0-macos-universal.dmg) |\n| Linux (KDE Plasma, GNOME, Sway, Hyprland) | [.deb](https://github.com/wallpaper-reactor/wallpaper-reactor-website/releases/download/v0.30.0/wallpaper-reactor-v0.30.0-linux-amd64.deb) · [Flatpak](https://github.com/wallpaper-reactor/wallpaper-reactor-website/releases/download/v0.30.0/wallpaper-reactor-v0.30.0-linux-amd64.flatpak) |\n"
